        </ul>

        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Measure everything — boards, railings at 3.5 square feet per foot, stairs, fascia — and expect the total to be roughly double the floor. Divide by a realistic coverage rate for your product and your wood, add a second coat at about 40 per cent better coverage, and then add 15 per cent on top.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            For the common 12 by 16 deck with rails and steps, that means 4 gallons of penetrating oil or 3 gallons of water-based or solid stain. Buy it all at once in matching lots, box the cans, and keep the leftover for touch-ups. The spare gallon is the cheapest insurance on the job.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
